# ---- renv --------------------------------------------------------------------
# renv writes and maintains renv/.gitignore, which excludes library/, sandbox/,
# staging/ and friends. renv.lock, renv/activate.R and renv/settings.json are
# tracked on purpose — they are what makes a clean checkout reproducible.

# ---- Quarto ------------------------------------------------------------------
.quarto/

# The rendered site. Not committed to main — `quarto publish gh-pages` builds
# it and pushes it to the gh-pages branch, which is the branch GitHub serves.
/_book/

# Chapters render to their source directory before Quarto moves them into
# _book, so a failed render can leave them behind. No leading slash: chapters
# and appendices now live in subdirectories, and _book/ is ignored separately,
# so unanchored is what catches the strays without touching the output.
*_files/

# _freeze/ IS committed, on purpose: it lets a clean checkout rebuild the book
# without re-running every R chunk.

